From 997e37142dbe1cc36f3c57b97803e5ed1bb4901d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:56:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Thylacine Warp vkQuake-arc W-3e: the warp-ctx-pub getter +
 the SDL first-frame witness

Two pieces of the SDL2 Vulkan glue chunk that live mesa-side:

1. vn_renderer_thylacine_warp_ctx_pub() -- the connected renderer's warp
   ctx public id as a process-global (set at warp_open, cleared at destroy
   only if still ours; raw value, since the server never mints pub 0).
   The SDL window glue needs it for the consent's SURFACE half: the
   tapestry surface's `glsrc <ctx>` must name this ctx for the mutual
   adoption to complete. Companion to the existing set_surface global
   (the ctx half), same single-renderer deployment posture.

2. thylacine-vk-sdl-prove -- the W-3e witness: an ordinary SDL2 Vulkan
   app (SDL_CreateWindow(SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN) -> SDL_Vulkan_* -> headless
   surface -> the W-3d swapchain) that renders the W-1 SPIR-V triangle
   INTO a display-sized presentable through a real render pass, verifies
   the pixels by copy-out (center red / corner blue -- the pair is the
   control), and presents 3 frames whose pokes complete the two-sided
   consent to a DIRECT scanout bind. Pre-window failures degrade to
   ABSENT (the probe rides every boot; the venus gate requires PASS on
   the leg with the capability). Links the pouch libSDL2.a (same musl
   target as this cross env) found beside the build tree; the link
   carries -Wl,-u,vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr because the app's only venus
   references are SDL's WEAK ones and a weak ref does not extract
   archive members -- the same line every SDL-only Vulkan app (vkQuake)
   needs, proven here rather than documented untested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/meson.build              |  28 +
 src/virtio/vulkan/thylacine_vk_sdl_prove.c | 843 +++++++++++++++++++++
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer.h            |   7 +
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_thylacine.c  |  23 +-
 4 files changed, 900 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/virtio/vulkan/thylacine_vk_sdl_prove.c

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/meson.build b/src/virtio/vulkan/meson.build
index 93dc32a..71256c6 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -204,4 +204,32 @@ if with_thylacine
     dependencies : vn_deps,
     install : false,
   )
+
+  # W-3e: the SDL2 Vulkan-glue witness -- an ordinary SDL app driving the
+  # SDL_thylacinevulkan hooks into the W-3d swapchain (the first-Vulkan-frame
+  # witness). Links the pouch cross-built libSDL2.a shipped beside the build
+  # tree (the mesa cross env IS the pouch sysroot -- same musl target); built
+  # only when that archive is present, so a venus-prove-only build tree is
+  # unaffected.
+  thy_sdl2_dir = '/build/sdl2'
+  thy_sdl2_lib = meson.get_compiler('c').find_library(
+    'SDL2', dirs : [thy_sdl2_dir + '/lib'], required : false)
+  if thy_sdl2_lib.found()
+    thylacine_vk_sdl_prove = executable(
+      'thylacine-vk-sdl-prove',
+      files('thylacine_vk_sdl_prove.c'),
+      include_directories : vn_incs,
+      c_args : ['-I' + thy_sdl2_dir + '/include/SDL2'],
+      # -u: the app reaches Vulkan only through SDL_Vulkan_* (the honest
+      # app shape), whose venus references are WEAK -- and a weak ref does
+      # not extract archive members, so without this the ICD entry stays
+      # NULL and LoadLibrary reports no-ICD at run time. This is the same
+      # link line every SDL-only Vulkan app (vkQuake) needs; the witness
+      # exercising it is the recipe's proof.
+      link_args : ['-Wl,-u,vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr'],
+      link_with : libvulkan_virtio,
+      dependencies : [vn_deps, thy_sdl2_lib],
+      install : false,
+    )
+  endif
 endif
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/thylacine_vk_sdl_prove.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/thylacine_vk_sdl_prove.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bba1f01
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/thylacine_vk_sdl_prove.c
@@ -0,0 +1,843 @@
+/*
+ * Copyright 2026 The Thylacine Authors
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+ *
+ * W-3e: the first-Vulkan-frame witness -- an SDL2 program.
+ *
+ * thylacine_prove.c drives the venus driver bare (step 10 proved the W-3d
+ * swapchain machinery with the present poke DORMANT -- no tapestry surface
+ * named).  This binary is the missing half: an ordinary SDL2 Vulkan app
+ * shape -- SDL_CreateWindow(SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN) -> SDL_Vulkan_* glue
+ * (SDL_thylacinevulkan.c) -> headless surface -> the W-3d swapchain -- that
+ * ARMS the two-sided display consent at SDL_Vulkan_CreateSurface (the
+ * window's tapestry surface accepts the warp ctx via glsrc; the renderer's
+ * present poke names the surface back), renders the W-1 triangle INTO a
+ * presentable through a real render pass, verifies the pixels by copy-out,
+ * and presents -- so every vkQueuePresentKHR pokes `present-to ... img` and
+ * the compositor DIRECT-binds the presentable to the scanout.  The app-side
+ * PASS line pairs with tapestryd's `scanout direct ... img res ...` line;
+ * TOGETHER they are the witness that a Vulkan frame reached the display.
+ *
+ * Window size = the display size (SDL desktop mode = the compositor's
+ * `display W H`): the DIRECT accept set admits a display-sized presentable,
+ * and a mismatch would leave the presents display-inert (the composed arm
+ * is not built), failing the compositor-line half of the gate.
+ *
+ * The loader-less pattern, same as thylacine_prove.c: instance-parented
+ * entrypoints via vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr (here reached through
+ * SDL_Vulkan_GetVkGetInstanceProcAddr -- proving SDL's handoff), device-
+ * parented ones as direct vn_/wsi_/vk_common symbols (the gipa trampolines
+ * for those load loader-populated dispatch slots this static link never
+ * fills).  The SDL link needs no -u: this file's direct vn_* references
+ * extract the driver archive members themselves.
+ */
+
